---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="A free infrastructure review to find practical improvements across cost, security, reliability, and delivery speed." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Free Infrastructure Review | Amir Hossein Rassafi" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Find low-effort infrastructure improvements that reduce cost and risk while helping teams ship faster." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://amir-h-rassafi.github.io/consultation/" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://amir-h-rassafi.github.io/consultation/" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/4.7.0/css/font-awesome.min.css" />
    <title>Free Infrastructure Review | Amir Hossein Rassafi</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="topbar">
      <nav class="topnav" aria-label="Site navigation">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
        <a class="infra-review" href="/consultation/" aria-current="page">Free Infra Review</a>
        <a class="subscribe social-media-items" data-link-id="gmail" href="https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=amir.rassafi@gmail.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="consultation-page">
      <section class="consultation-hero" aria-labelledby="consultation-title">
        <div class="consultation-hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Free 30-minute infrastructure review</p>
          <h1 id="consultation-title">Infrastructure should create momentum, not drag.</h1>
          <p class="consultation-lede">A good platform does not force a choice between saving money, staying secure, and shipping quickly. It creates a practical balance—then keeps evolving with the product.</p>
          <form class="consultation-actions" id="consultation-form">
            <button class="action action--primary" type="submit">Request a free review</button>
            <span>No pitch. Just a useful second opinion.</span>
          </form>
        </div>

        <aside class="review-card" aria-label="What the review covers">
          <p class="review-card-label">A healthy foundation</p>
          <div class="review-scorecard">
            <div><span>01</span><strong>Cost</strong><small>Spend with intent</small></div>
            <div><span>02</span><strong>Security</strong><small>Reduce real risk</small></div>
            <div><span>03</span><strong>Change</strong><small>Evolve without fear</small></div>
            <div><span>04</span><strong>Speed</strong><small>Ship with confidence</small></div>
          </div>
          <p class="review-card-note">The goal is not “perfect infrastructure.” It is the right infrastructure for the business today—with a safe path forward.</p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="consultation-balance" aria-labelledby="balance-title">
        <div class="consultation-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The real target</p>
          <h2 id="balance-title">Better outcomes, not more infrastructure.</h2>
          <p>Architecture earns its keep when it helps the whole organisation. Every recommendation should improve at least one outcome without quietly undermining the others.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-grid">
          <article><span>Cost</span><h3>Spend where it matters</h3><p>Remove waste, right-size resources, and make future costs easier to understand.</p></article>
          <article><span>Security</span><h3>Protect the likely paths</h3><p>Strengthen access, secrets, backups, and recovery before adding complex controls.</p></article>
          <article><span>Adaptability</span><h3>Keep change affordable</h3><p>Reduce brittle dependencies so the platform can grow with the product and team.</p></article>
          <article><span>Delivery</span><h3>Shorten the path to value</h3><p>Make releases repeatable, observable, and safe enough to happen more often.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="quick-wins" aria-labelledby="quick-wins-title">
        <div class="quick-wins-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Start with the obvious wins</p>
          <h2 id="quick-wins-title">There is usually valuable work hiding in plain sight.</h2>
          <p>Many improvements do not need a migration, a new platform, or months of effort. A review should surface the low-hanging fruit first: small, safe changes that pay back quickly and create room for the work that follows.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="quick-wins-list">
          <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Unused and oversized resources</strong><p>Stop paying for capacity the product does not use.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Manual release steps</strong><p>Automate the repeated parts that slow delivery and invite mistakes.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Weak visibility</strong><p>Add the few signals that make failures faster to find and fix.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Access and backup gaps</strong><p>Close common risks with clear ownership and tested recovery.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ai-operations" aria-labelledby="ai-operations-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">AI with guardrails</p>
          <h2 id="ai-operations-title">Keep the system under control without creating more work.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-operations-copy">
          <p>Used carefully, AI can reduce the routine effort of running infrastructure: reviewing changes, improving documentation, investigating incidents, and keeping configuration consistent.</p>
          <p>It should support engineering judgement—not bypass it. Clear boundaries, reviewable changes, and existing security controls keep the benefit high and the risk low.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="consultation-cta" aria-labelledby="consultation-cta-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A practical first step</p>
          <h2 id="consultation-cta-title">Find the first few improvements worth making.</h2>
        </div>
        <button class="action action--primary" type="submit" form="consultation-form">Request a free review</button>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script is:inline async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-7B9L2V5DRV"></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
      gtag('js', new Date());
      gtag('config', 'G-7B9L2V5DRV');


      var trackedLinks = document.getElementsByClassName('social-media-items');
      var useMailApp = window.matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches;
      if (useMailApp) {
        var contactLink = document.querySelector('[data-link-id="gmail"]');
        contactLink.href = 'mailto:amir.rassafi@gmail.com';
        contactLink.removeAttribute('target');
        contactLink.removeAttribute('rel');
      }
      for (var i = 0; i < trackedLinks.length; i++) {
        trackedLinks[i].addEventListener('click', function() {
          gtag('event', 'click', {
            event_category: 'Link Clicks',
            event_label: this.getAttribute('data-link-id')
          });
        });
      }
    </script>
    <script is:inline>
      document.getElementById('consultation-form').addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
        event.preventDefault();
        var subject = encodeURIComponent('Free infrastructure review');
        var body = encodeURIComponent('Hi Amir,\n\nI\x27d like to request a free infrastructure review.\n\nA little context:\n- Company or project:\n- Current infrastructure or cloud provider:\n- Main challenge:\n- Approximate monthly infrastructure spend (optional):\n\nBest,\n');
        gtag('event', 'consultation_email', { event_category: 'Consultation', event_label: 'free_infrastructure_review' });
        if (useMailApp) {
          window.location.href = 'mailto:amir.rassafi@gmail.com?subject=' + subject + '&body=' + body;
          return;
        }
        window.open('https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=amir.rassafi@gmail.com&su=' + subject + '&body=' + body, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer');
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
